---
import site from '../data/site.json';

const nav = [
  { label: 'Events', href: '/events' },
  { label: 'About', href: '/about' },
  { label: 'Get involved', href: '/get-involved' },
  { label: 'Sponsor', href: '/sponsor' },
];

const path = Astro.url.pathname;
const isCurrent = (href: string) => path === href || path.startsWith(`${href}/`);

/* Frosted capsule — a translucent white wash, a hairline highlight edge and a
   navy label. Where backdrop-filter is supported the wash thins out and the
   blur does the rest of the work; where it isn't, the wash stays a step
   heavier so the label still clears AA on its own. See the comment block below
   for the composited numbers. */
const frost = [
  'bg-white/30 ring-1 ring-inset ring-white/60',
  'supports-[backdrop-filter]:bg-white/25 supports-[backdrop-filter]:backdrop-blur-md',
  'hover:bg-white/50 supports-[backdrop-filter]:hover:bg-white/45',
].join(' ');
---

{/* Header — Variant B banner (style guide cyan → purple → pink), nav styled as
    frosted glass: the gradient reads straight through the nav chrome, so each
    item picks up whichever part of the run it sits over. Same idea as the haze
    over the river in the hero art rather than the hard pixels of the skyline.

    The banner gradient and the navy PERTH AI wordmark pill are settled — don't
    change them. Everything below is about the nav.

    CONTRAST — composited, not eyeballed. A translucent fill mixes with the
    gradient beneath it, so every number here is the label against the ACTUAL
    composited background at the worst point of the run. Raw on the gradient,
    nothing survives: ink-950 is 9.57:1 on azure-500 and 7.27:1 on coral-500
    but only 3.46:1 on orchid-500 in the middle, and white is 5.71:1 on orchid
    but 2.07:1 / 2.72:1 at the ends. orchid-500 (#7B3FE4) is therefore the
    worst case for every frosted element, and it is the only one worth quoting.

      white/30 over orchid-500  → #A2789A-ish composite, L 0.2738
                                  ink-950 label 6.11:1   (no-blur base state)
      white/25 over orchid-500  → L 0.2437
                                  ink-950 label 5.54:1   (blur-supported state)
      white/45 hover            → ~8.4:1
      white/85 mobile panel     → ≥14.2:1 even over solid ink-950, so the panel
                                  is safe over the hero art and over page copy

    So the base, unblurred state clears 4.5:1 by itself (6.11:1) and the thinner
    blurred state still clears it (5.54:1). Both have to pass independently:
    Tailwind compiles supports-[backdrop-filter] to a `backdrop-filter:var(--tw)`
    probe, and @supports treats any var() as valid syntax, so that query is
    effectively always true and the thin wash can land on a browser with no
    blur at all. Don't thin it further either — white/15 measures 4.54:1 over
    orchid, which is inside the rounding.

    Active and CTA are OPAQUE on purpose — that is what makes them win against
    translucent neighbours. Desktop active is a solid white capsule (ink-950
    label, 19.8:1); the CTA is solid sunbeam cream (ink-950 label, 17.0:1). On
    the mobile panel the panel itself is near-white, so an opaque white capsule
    would disappear — the active item there is an orchid-500 fill with a white
    label (5.71:1, measured) instead.

    Focus: the global :focus-visible ring is sunset-500 orange, which this
    banner doesn't use. Items on the gradient take an ink-950 ring (3.46:1 at
    worst, clears the 3:1 a non-text indicator needs); items inside the navy
    wordmark pill or on the orchid fill take a white ring. */}
<header class="sticky top-0 z-40 border-b border-ink-950/25 bg-gradient-to-r from-azure-500 via-orchid-500 to-coral-500">
  <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-6xl items-center gap-4 px-5 py-3 sm:px-8">
    <a
      href="/"
      class="rounded-full bg-ink-950 px-4 py-2 font-display text-lg font-bold tracking-tight text-white shadow-sm shadow-ink-950/30 focus-visible:outline-white"
    >
      PERTH <span class="text-azure-400">AI</span>
      <span class="sr-only">— home</span>
    </a>

    <nav aria-label="Main" class="ml-auto hidden items-center gap-2 md:flex">
      {
        nav.map((item) => (
          <a
            href={item.href}
            aria-current={isCurrent(item.href) ? 'page' : undefined}
            class:list={[
              'rounded-full px-3.5 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-ink-950 transition focus-visible:outline-ink-950',
              isCurrent(item.href)
                ? 'bg-white shadow-sm shadow-ink-950/25 ring-1 ring-inset ring-white'
                : frost,
            ]}
          >
            {item.label}
          </a>
        ))
      }
    </nav>

    <a
      href={site.links.luma}
      class="hidden rounded-full bg-sunbeam-400 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-ink-950 shadow-sm shadow-ink-950/25 ring-1 ring-inset ring-white/70 transition-colors hover:bg-white focus-visible:outline-ink-950 md:block"
    >
      Next event
    </a>

    <!-- Mobile menu: <details> so it works with zero JavaScript -->
    <details class="group relative ml-auto md:hidden">
      <summary
        class:list={[
          'flex cursor-pointer items-center gap-2 rounded-full px-3.5 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-ink-950 transition marker:content-none focus-visible:outline-ink-950 [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden',
          frost,
          'group-open:bg-white group-open:ring-white',
        ]}
      >
        <span>Menu</span>
        <svg
          class="h-4 w-4 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180"
          viewBox="0 0 20 20"
          fill="currentColor"
          aria-hidden="true"
        >
          <path
            fill-rule="evenodd"
            d="M5.22 8.22a.75.75 0 0 1 1.06 0L10 11.94l3.72-3.72a.75.75 0 1 1 1.06 1.06l-4.25 4.25a.75.75 0 0 1-1.06 0L5.22 9.28a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.06Z"
            clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
        </svg>
      </summary>
      <nav
        aria-label="Main"
        class="absolute right-0 mt-2 w-56 rounded-2xl bg-white/85 p-2 shadow-lg shadow-ink-950/30 ring-1 ring-inset ring-white supports-[backdrop-filter]:backdrop-blur-lg"
      >
        {
          nav.map((item) => (
            <a
              href={item.href}
              aria-current={isCurrent(item.href) ? 'page' : undefined}
              class:list={[
                'block rounded-xl px-3 py-2 text-sm font-semibold transition',
                isCurrent(item.href)
                  ? 'bg-orchid-500 text-white focus-visible:outline-white'
                  : 'text-ink-950 hover:bg-orchid-100 focus-visible:outline-ink-950',
              ]}
            >
              {item.label}
            </a>
          ))
        }
        <a
          href={site.links.luma}
          class="mt-1 block rounded-xl bg-ink-950 px-3 py-2 text-center text-sm font-semibold text-white focus-visible:outline-ink-950"
        >
          Next event
        </a>
      </nav>
    </details>
  </div>
</header>
